{"subjectId":"dsa-advanced","id":"searching","title":"Searching","group":"","order":4,"html":"<section class=\"block\"><h3>Search in an Infinite Sorted Array</h3>\n<div class=\"callout callout--example\">\n<div class=\"callout-label\"><i class=\"ti ti-terminal-2\"></i> Case Example</div>\n<p><strong>Input:</strong> arr[] = {10, 15, 20, 40, 80, 80, 90, 100, 120, ........ } ; x = 100<br><strong>Output:</strong> 7</p>\n</div>\n<p>I/p : arr[] = {20, 40, 10, 30, ........ } ; x = 50</p>\n<div class=\"callout callout--example\">\n<div class=\"callout-label\"><i class=\"ti ti-terminal-2\"></i> Case Example</div>\n<p><strong>Output:</strong> -1</p>\n</div>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code># Naive Solution\n\ndef search(arr, x):\n  i = 0\n  while True:\n    if arr[i] == x:\n      return i\n\n    if arr[i] &gt; x:\n      return -1\n\n    i += 1\n\narr = [10, 15, 20, 40, 80, 80, 90, 100, 120]\nprint(search(arr, 50))\nprint(search(arr, 80))\n\n# Auxiliary Space : O(1)</code></pre></figure>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code># Efficient Solution\n\ndef bsearch(arr, low, high, x):\n    while low &lt;= high:\n        mid = (low + high) // 2\n        if arr[mid] == x:\n            return mid\n        elif arr[mid] &lt; x:\n            low = mid + 1\n        else:\n            high = mid - 1\n    return -1\n\ndef search(arr, x):\n  if arr[0] == x:\n    return 0\n  i = 1\n  while arr[i] &lt; x:\n    i = i * 2\n    if arr[i] == x:\n      return i\n  return bsearch(arr, i//2 + 1, i - 1, x)\n\narr = [10, 15, 20, 40, 80, 80, 90, 100, 120]\nprint(search(arr, 50))\nprint(search(arr, 40))\n\n# Auxiliary Space : O(1)</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3>Search in a Sorted Rotated Array</h3>\n<div class=\"callout callout--example\">\n<div class=\"callout-label\"><i class=\"ti ti-terminal-2\"></i> Case Example</div>\n<p><strong>Input:</strong> arr[] = {10, 20, 30, 40, 50, 8, 9} ; x = 30<br><strong>Output:</strong> 2<br><strong>Input:</strong> arr[] = {100, 200, 300, 10, 20} ; x = 40<br><strong>Output:</strong> -1</p>\n</div>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code># Naive Solution\n\ndef search(arr, n, x):\n  for i in range(n):\n    if arr[i] == x:\n      return i\n\n  return -1\n\narr = [10, 20, 30, 40, 50, 8, 9]\nn = len(arr)\nx = 30\n\nsearch(arr, n, x)\n\n# Auxiliary Space : O(1)</code></pre></figure>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code># Efficient Solution\n\ndef search(arr, n, x):\n  low = 0\n  high = n -1\n\n  while low &lt;= high:\n    mid = (low + high) // 2\n\n    if arr[mid] == x:\n      return mid\n\n    if arr[low] &lt; arr[mid]:\n\n      if arr[low] &lt;= x and x &lt; arr[mid]:\n        high = mid - 1\n      else:\n        low = mid + 1\n\n    else:\n\n      if arr[mid] &lt; x and x &lt;= arr[high]:\n        low = mid + 1\n      else:\n        high = mid - 1\n\n  return - 1\n\narr = [10, 20, 30, 40, 50, 8, 9]\nn = len(arr)\nx = 8\nsearch(arr, n, x)\n\n# Auxiliary Space : O(1)</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3>Find a Peak Element : Not Smaller than Neighbour</h3>\n<div class=\"callout callout--example\">\n<div class=\"callout-label\"><i class=\"ti ti-terminal-2\"></i> Case Example</div>\n<p><strong>Input:</strong> arr[] = {5, 10, 20, 15, 7}<br><strong>Output:</strong> 20<br><strong>Input:</strong> arr[] = {10, 20, 15, 5, 23, 90, 67}<br><strong>Output:</strong> 20 or 90</p>\n</div>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code># Naive Solution\n\ndef getPeak(arr, n):\n  if n == 1:\n    return arr[0]\n\n  if arr[0] &gt;= arr[1]:\n    return arr[0]\n\n  if arr[n-1] &gt;= arr[n-2]:\n    return arr[n-1]\n\n  for i in range(1, n - 1):\n    if arr[i] &gt;= arr[i-1] and arr[i] &gt;= arr[i+1]:\n      return arr[i]\n\narr = [10, 20, 15, 5, 23, 90, 67]\nn = len(arr)\ngetPeak(arr, n)\n\n# Auxiliary Space : O(1)</code></pre></figure>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code># Efficient Solution\n\ndef getPeak(arr, n):\n  low = 0\n  high = n - 1\n\n  while low &lt;= high:\n\n    mid = (low + high)//2\n\n    if ((mid == 0 or arr[mid-1] &lt;= arr[mid]) and (mid == n-1 or arr[mid+1] &lt;= arr[mid])):\n      return arr[mid]\n\n    elif mid &gt; 0 and arr[mid-1] &gt;= arr[mid]:\n      high = mid - 1\n\n    else:\n\n      low = mid + 1\n\narr = [10, 20, 15, 5, 23, 90, 67]\nn = len(arr)\ngetPeak(arr, n)\n\n# Auxiliary Space : O(1)</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3>Two Pointer Approach</h3>\n<p>Example : Find if there is a pair with sum in sorted array</p>\n<div class=\"callout callout--example\">\n<div class=\"callout-label\"><i class=\"ti ti-terminal-2\"></i> Case Example</div>\n<p><strong>Input:</strong> arr[] = [2, 5, 8, 12, 30] ; x = 17<br><strong>Output:</strong> True<br><strong>Input:</strong> arr[] = [3, 8, 13, 18] ; x = 14<br><strong>Output:</strong> False</p>\n</div>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code># Naive Solution\n\ndef isPair(arr, x):\n  n = len(arr)\n\n  for i in range(n-1):\n    for j in range(i+1, n):\n      if arr[i] + arr[j] == x:\n        return True\n\n  return False\n\narr =  [2, 5, 8, 12, 30]\nx = 17\nisPair(arr, x)\n\n# Auxiliary Space : O(1)</code></pre></figure>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code># Idea for Efficient Solution\n\ndef isPair(arr, x):\n  i = 0\n  j = len(arr) - 1\n\n  while i &lt; j:\n    if arr[i] + arr[j] == x:\n      return True\n\n    elif arr[i] + arr[j] &lt; x:\n      i = i + 1\n\n    else:\n\n      j = j - 1\n\n  return False\n\narr =  [2, 5, 8, 12, 30]\nx = 17\nisPair(arr, x)\n\n# Auxiliary Space : O(1)</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3>Triplet in a Sorted Array</h3>\n<div class=\"callout callout--example\">\n<div class=\"callout-label\"><i class=\"ti ti-terminal-2\"></i> Case Example</div>\n<p><strong>Input:</strong> arr[] = [2, 3, 4, 8, 9, 20, 40] ; x = 32<br><strong>Output:</strong> True<br><strong>Input:</strong> arr[] = [1, 2, 5, 6] ; x = 14<br><strong>Output:</strong> False</p>\n</div>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code># Naive Solution\n\ndef isTriplet(arr, x):\n  n = len(arr)\n\n  for i in range(n):\n    for j in range(i+1, n):\n      for k in range(j+1, n):\n        if arr[i] + arr[j] + arr[k] == x:\n          return True\n\n  return False\n\narr = [2, 3, 4, 8, 9, 20, 40]\nx = 9\nisTriplet(arr, x)\n\n# Auxiliary Space : O(1)</code></pre></figure>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code># Efficient Solution\n'''\n1. Traverse the array from left to right\n2. For Every element arr[i], check if there is a pair on right side with sum(x-arr[i])\n'''\n\ndef isPair(arr, x, si):\n  i = si\n  j = len(arr) - 1\n\n  while i &lt; j:\n    if arr[i] + arr[j] == x:\n      return True\n\n    elif arr[i] + arr[j] &lt; x:\n      i = i + 1\n\n    else:\n      j = j - 1\n\n  return False\n\ndef isTriplet(arr, x):\n  for i in range(len(arr) - 2):\n    if isPair(arr, x-arr[i], i+1):\n      return True\n  return False\n\narr = [2, 3, 4, 8, 9, 20, 40]\nx = 9\nisTriplet(arr, x)\n\n# Auxiliary Space : O(1)</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3>Median of Two Sorted Arrays</h3>\n<div class=\"callout callout--example\">\n<div class=\"callout-label\"><i class=\"ti ti-terminal-2\"></i> Case Example</div>\n<p><strong>Input:</strong> arr1[] = {10, 20, 30, 40, 50} ; arr2 = {5, 15, 25, 35, 45}<br><strong>Output:</strong> 27.5<br><strong>Input:</strong> arr1[] = {1, 2, 3} ; arr2[] = {4, 5, 6}<br><strong>Output:</strong> 3.5</p>\n</div>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code># Naive Solution\n\ndef findMedianSortedArrays(A1, A2):\n    # Step 1: Merge the two sorted arrays\n    merged = []\n    i, j = 0, 0\n    m, n = len(A1), len(A2)\n\n    while i &lt; m and j &lt; n:\n        if A1[i] &lt;= A2[j]:\n            merged.append(A1[i])\n            i += 1\n        else:\n            merged.append(A2[j])\n            j += 1\n\n    # Append any remaining elements\n    while i &lt; m:\n        merged.append(A1[i])\n        i += 1\n\n    while j &lt; n:\n        merged.append(A2[j])\n        j += 1\n\n    # Step 2: Find the median\n    total_length = len(merged)\n    mid = total_length // 2\n\n    if total_length % 2 == 1:\n        # Odd length: return the middle element\n        return merged[mid]\n    else:\n        # Even length: return the average of the two middle elements\n        return (merged[mid - 1] + merged[mid]) / 2\n\n# Example usage\nA1 = [1, 3, 5]\nA2 = [2, 4, 6, 8, 10]\nprint(findMedianSortedArrays(A1, A2))  # Output: 4.0</code></pre></figure>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code># Efficient Solution\n\ndef getMed(a1, a2):\n  n1, n2 = len(a1), len(a2)\n  b1, e1 = 0, n1\n\n  while b1 &lt;= e1:\n    i1 = (b1 + e1) // 2\n    i2 = (n1 + n2 + 1) // 2 - i1\n\n    mnr1 = float(\"inf\") if i1 == n1 else a1[i1]\n    mxl1 = float(\"inf\") if i1 == 0 else a1[i1-1]\n\n    mnr2 = a2[i2]\n    mxl2 = a2[i2-1]\n\n    if mxl1 &lt;= mnr2 and mxl2 &lt;= mnr1:\n\n      if (n1 + n2) % 2 == 0:\n        return (max(mxl1, mxl2) + min(mnr1, mnr2)) / 2\n      else:\n        return max(mxl1, mxl2)\n\n    elif mxl1 &gt; mnr2:\n      e1 = i1 - 1\n\n    else:\n      b1 = i1 + 1\n\nA1 = [1, 3, 5]\nA2 = [2, 4, 6, 8, 10]\nprint(getMed(A1, A2))</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3>Repeating Element</h3>\n<p>-&gt; Array Size, n &gt;= 2</p>\n<p>-&gt; Only one element Repeats (Any number of Times)</p>\n<p>-&gt; All the Elements from o to max(arr) are present</p>\n<p>Therefore 0 &lt;= max(arr) &lt;= n-2</p>\n<p>-------------</p>\n<div class=\"callout callout--example\">\n<div class=\"callout-label\"><i class=\"ti ti-terminal-2\"></i> Case Example</div>\n<p><strong>Input:</strong> arr[] = {0, 2, 1, 3, 2, 2}<br><strong>Output:</strong> 2</p>\n</div>\n<p>-------------</p>\n<p>-&gt; O(n) Time</p>\n<p>-&gt; O(1) Aux Space</p>\n<p>-&gt; No Modifications to Original Array</p>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code># Naive Solution : Sort the Array\n\narr = [0, 1, 2, 2, 2, 3, 2, 4, 6, 6, 6]\n\narr = sorted(arr)\nprint(arr)\nn = len(arr)\n\nfor i in range(0, n-2):\n  if arr[i] == arr[i+1]:\n    print(arr[i])\n\n# Auxiliary Space : O(1)</code></pre></figure>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code># Super Naive\n\narr = [0, 1, 2, 2, 2, 3, 2, 4, 6, 6, 6]\n\nseen = set()\nduplicates = set()\n\nfor num in arr:\n    if num in seen:\n        duplicates.add(num)\n    else:\n        seen.add(num)\n\nprint(duplicates)\n\n# Auxiliary Space : O(1)</code></pre></figure>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code># Efficient Solution\n\ndef repeat(arr, n):\n  visit = [False] * n\n  for i in range(n):\n    if visit[arr[i]]:\n      return arr[i]\n    visit[arr[i]] = True\n\n  return -1\n\narr = [0, 1, 2, 2, 2, 3, 2, 4, 6, 6, 6]\nn = len(arr)\n\nrepeat(arr, n)\n\n# Auxiliary Space : O(n)</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3>Repeating Element O(n) Time, O(1) Space and No Changes to array</h3>\n<div class=\"callout callout--example\">\n<div class=\"callout-label\"><i class=\"ti ti-terminal-2\"></i> Case Example</div>\n<p><strong>Input:</strong> arr[] = {1, 3, 2, 4, 3, 3}<br><strong>Output:</strong> 3<br><strong>Input:</strong> arr[] = {1, 1}<br><strong>Output:</strong> 1</p>\n</div>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code># Method\n\ndef repeat1(arr, n):\n    slow = arr[0]\n    fast = arr[0]\n\n    slow = arr[slow]\n    fast = arr[arr[fast]]\n\n    while slow != fast:\n        slow = arr[slow]\n        fast = arr[arr[fast]]\n\n    slow = arr[0]\n\n    while slow != fast:\n        slow = arr[slow]\n        fast = arr[fast]\n\n    return slow\n\narr = [1, 3, 4, 2, 2]\nn = len(arr) - 1\n\nprint(repeat1(arr, n))</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3>Allocate Minimum No.of Pages</h3>\n<div class=\"callout callout--example\">\n<div class=\"callout-label\"><i class=\"ti ti-terminal-2\"></i> Case Example</div>\n<p><strong>Input:</strong> arr[] = {10, 20, 30, 40} ; k = 2<br><strong>Output:</strong> 60<br><strong>Input:</strong> arr[] = {10, 20, 30} ; k = 1<br><strong>Output:</strong> 60</p>\n</div>\n<p>-&gt; Minimize the maximum pages allocated</p>\n<p>-&gt; Only contiguous pages can be allocated</p>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code># Naive Recursive Solution\n\n'''\nx0 | x1 | x2 | ....... | xi - 1 | xi | ....... | xn-1\n\nwe need to choose (k-1) cuts out of (n-1) cuts shown above\n\n\n              n-1\nTotal Ways :     C\n                  k-1\n\nEx: [10, 20, 30, 40] ; k = 2\n\nWe need to choose 1 cut out of 3 cuts\n'''\n\ndef minPages(arr, n, k):\n  if k == 1:\n    return sum(arr[0:n])\n\n  if n == 1:\n    return arr[0]\n\n  res = float('inf')\n\n  for i in range(1, n):\n    res = min(res, max(minPages(arr, i, k-1), sum(arr[i : n])))\n\n  return res\n\narr = [10, 20, 30, 40]\nk = 2\nn = len(arr)\n\nminPages(arr, n, k)</code></pre></figure>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code># Efficient Solution\n\ndef minPages(arr, k):\n  n = len(arr)\n  s = sum(arr)\n  mx = max(arr)\n\n  low, high = mx, s\n  res = 0\n\n  while low &lt;= high:\n    mid = (low + high) // 2\n\n    if isFeasible(arr, k, mid):\n      res = mid\n      high = mid - 1\n    else:\n      low = mid + 1\n\n  return res\n\ndef isFeasible(arr, k, ans):\n  req, s = 1, 0\n  for i in range(n):\n    if s + arr[i] &gt; ans:\n      req += 1\n      s = arr[i]\n    else:\n      s += arr[i]\n\n  return req &lt;= k\n\narr = [10, 20, 30, 40]\nk = 2\nn = len(arr)\n\nminPages(arr, k)</code></pre></figure></section>"}